        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In 2015, Nohemi Gonzalez, a U. S. citizen, was killed in a set of coordinated terrorist attacks carried out across Paris, France, under the direction of the Islamic State of Iraq and Syria (ISIS)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiffs",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe76c1f6e8ed6b17d3a6a0bd8f602ee9a5f1a361aa25faad62e6caf2be65b647",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe76c1f6e8ed-0000-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Plaintiffs alleged that Google aided and abetted and conspired with ISIS through ISIS' use of YouTube, which Google owns and operates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe76c1f6e8ed6b17d3a6a0bd8f602ee9a5f1a361aa25faad62e6caf2be65b647",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe76c1f6e8ed-0000-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Deputy Solicitor General Stewart argued the cause for the United States as amicus curiae urging vacatur."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe76c1f6e8ed6b17d3a6a0bd8f602ee9a5f1a361aa25faad62e6caf2be65b647",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe76c1f6e8ed-0000-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We granted certiorari to review the Ninth Circuit's application of \u00a7 230."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe76c1f6e8ed6b17d3a6a0bd8f602ee9a5f1a361aa25faad62e6caf2be65b647",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe76c1f6e8ed-0000-0004",
      "kind": "holding",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Since we hold that the complaint in that case fails to state a claim for aiding and abetting under \u00a7 2333(d)(2), it appears to follow that the complaint here likewise fails to state such a claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1333",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "fe76c1f6e8ed6b17d3a6a0bd8f602ee9a5f1a361aa25faad62e6caf2be65b647",
      "evidence_id": "ev-fe76c1f6e8ed-0000-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": "per_curiam",
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We therefore decline to address the application of \u00a7 230 to a complaint that appears to state little, if any, plausible claim for relief. Instead, we vacate the judgment below and remand the case for the Ninth Circuit to consider plaintiffs' complaint in light of our decision in Twitter."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
